<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Known Issues in KUBE</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<ol start="1" class="whs4">
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Open: drag and drop *.asc file to the KUBE shortcut on the desktop, then open it as point cloud. This will cause the application not responding.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Align to plane in inspection mode: all labels set in the view remain in the aligned 2D section, even though these don’t belong to the section.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When scanning right or sharp edges there appear sometimes interlaced triangles between both sides.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When the connection to MMIB-DL (for MMZ) is not available, a wrong message is issued saying that the MMIB is not connected to the SURFA PCI.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">If the localiser co-ordinates are locked during alignment, you cannot take any more points, or if it happens when you are capturing stripes the last frame of captured video is stuck in the calibrated view. To free up the arm again, you need to completely quit the alignment wizard, to turn laser OFF, then ON and restart alignment</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps"><span lang="EN-GB">An entity having</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>"</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">(double quotes) in its name can not be selected using the tree context menu command, because the quotation marks are used as special symbols in the macro commands.</span></p>
</li>
</ol>
